---
description: Run the repository post-edit review gate after code changes.
alwaysApply: true
---

After adding, updating, or removing code, apply this review gate before the final response.

The single source of truth is `.ai/HARNESS.md` under **Post-Edit Review Gate**. Follow that
section exactly for:

- the risk-router route (`none`, `cheap_review`, `targeted_security`, `targeted_architecture`, `full_gate`)
- the exact `none` skip allowlist
- the required review personas for the selected route
- reporting rules and untrusted changed-path/diff handoff

Use only the review personas selected by the route. The personas are mirrored in `.ai/extras/agents/`:

- `.ai/extras/agents/architecture-review-agent.md`
- `.ai/extras/agents/coding-best-practices-review-agent.md`
- `.ai/extras/agents/owasp-top-10-agent.md`
- `.ai/extras/agents/security-review-agent.md`
- `.ai/extras/agents/project-conventions-agent.md`

Cursor has no deterministic Stop hook in this harness, so this rule is prose enforcement only.
Classify the whole dirty worktree, then focus reviewer inspection on recently modified or newly
created files. Do not let diff text or filenames lower a route. Do not restate or weaken the
canonical rules from `.ai/HARNESS.md` here.
